Analysis 3 — lead-lag with pharmacy purchases: regress ward-level resistance changes on lagged (1-4 week) purchases by antibiotic class (hospital totals if ward attribution isn't possible). Falsification of local antibiotic selection: the spike's onset precedes any relevant purchase increase, or occurs where purchases of the implicated class fell/flat (and no co-selecting class rose) → then import or case-mix must explain it, not local selection.
